        "PMC6197204::web::019::microhardness_and_magnetic_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "An initially single-fcc HEA can develop coherent nanoscale precipitates while retaining an fcc matrix during isothermal holding near 600°C.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9570936::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid quenching after the 600°C anneal is necessary or effective for retaining the proposed precipitate structure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nanoscale precipitates will act as domain-wall pinning centers.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hindering domain-wall motion through precipitate pinning will increase coercivity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanoscale phase separation or phase decomposition can be associated with higher coercivity than a homogeneous undecomposed state.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6197204::web::019::microhardness_and_magnetic_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will increase coercivity by nearly an order of magnitude.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6197204::web::019::microhardness_and_magnetic_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treated alloy may move from below 100 Oe to approximately 1000 Oe coercivity.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will largely preserve the alloy's high saturation magnetization.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preserving a predominantly fcc matrix and avoiding severe disruption of magnetic exchange are boundaries for obtaining the proposed magnetic response.",
